message: "If you use CryptoBench, please cite it as below."
title: "CryptoBench: A benchmark of cryptographic API misuse for evaluating LLM code reviewers"
type: dataset
version: 1.0.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23067052
repository-code: "https://github.com/sunny-chokshi/cryptobench"
date-released: 2026-09-30
authors:
  - family-names: Chokshi
    given-names: Sunny
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-4738-7759"
    affiliation: "University of the Cumberlands"
license: "MIT AND CC-BY-4.0"
keywords:
  - cryptographic API misuse
  - vulnerability detection
  - large language models
  - code security
  - benchmark
abstract: >
  54 Python snippets covering nine cryptographic misuse classes (36 vulnerable,
  18 matched secure controls), a self-contained harness that queries local
  Ollama models, and 1,890 recorded trials across seven open code models.
